---
const asset = '/assets/projects/ssuperlative/';
const chapters = [
  {
    index: '01 / MOVEMENT & OBSERVATION',
    title: 'THINKING IN MOTION.',
    discipline: 'RUNNING / PERCEPTION / CREATIVE THINKING',
    copy: 'Running became a way to create rhythm, distance and room for thought. From 2019 onward, training records introduced movement, time and physiological measures into the investigation. The Human System also considers optic flow — how the visible world changes as we move through it — as a question about perception and creative thinking, not a proven causal explanation.',
  },
  {
    index: '02 / THE LIVING ARCHIVE',
    title: 'WRITING BECOMES A SYSTEM.',
    discipline: 'TYPED JOURNALS / VOICE / STRUCTURE',
    copy: 'Between 2021 and 2025, personal writing developed into an extensive archive. A memoir, daily entries and handwritten notes became both a means of reflection and a growing design problem: how to organise, retrieve and understand language at this scale. In 2025, dictation reopened the practice; voice introduced another form of recording, alongside later AI-assisted experiments in summarisation and reporting.',
  },
  {
    index: '04 / FROM DATA TO DESIGN',
    title: 'THE ARCHIVE BECOMES AN INTERFACE.',
    discipline: 'EARLY PRODUCT STUDIES / TIMELINES / DATA VISUALISATION',
    copy: 'The first journal and mood-interface studies emerged around 2023. Over time, the design expanded to bring running records, sleep, timelines and other observations into common structures. Visualising these relationships revealed new questions about hierarchy, context and the limitations of personal data. The point was not to diagnose from charts, but to test how design could make complex records easier to examine.',
  },
  {
    index: '05 / PROJECT ALICE',
    title: 'FROM RESEARCH TO A PRODUCT.',
    discipline: 'PRODUCT ARCHITECTURE / EDITORIAL REPORTING / PROTOTYPES',
    copy: 'Project Alice is the latest product-design chapter. Drawing on questions developed through years of observation, journaling and data experiments, it tests how timelines, measurements, narratives and source evidence might form a readable, connected report. The current prototype uses synthetic development data, allowing the information architecture, interaction and visual language to be explored without presenting the design as clinically validated.',
  },
  {
    index: '06 / AN EVOLVING PRACTICE',
    title: 'KEEP BECOMING.',
    discipline: 'OBSERVE / MAKE / REFLECT',
    copy: 'SSUPERLATIVE remains deliberately unfinished. It began as a personal inquiry, acquired a visual identity, grew through journals and data experiments, and now informs an evolving product. The work continues to move between making and understanding — with room for questions that no single chart, image or interface can settle.',
  },
];
---
<div class="ssuper-revised" data-source-frame="1836:2917">
  <div class="ssuper-inner">
    <figure class="ssuper-media ssuper-rope"><img src={`${asset}rope.png`} alt="Runner in motion above a cloud covered landscape" width="1344" height="896" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></figure>
    <h2 class="ssuper-opening">MOST BECOMING.</h2>
    <div class="ssuper-copy-row"><span>BECOMING</span><p>What became SSUPERLATIVE began before it had a name. From 2018, a personal investigation into the relationship between mind, body and identity evolved through movement, writing and observation. Around 2021, the word superlative gave this work an identity. What followed was a growing archive of experience — and an expanding design question: how can we give form to complexity without reducing the person behind it?</p></div>
    <figure class="ssuper-media"><img src={`${asset}identity-01.png`} alt="Black and white identity study" width="2912" height="1632" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></figure>
    <figure class="ssuper-media"><img src={`${asset}identity-02.png`} alt="Figure against a monumental architectural wall" width="1456" height="816" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></figure>

    <section class="ssuper-chapter" aria-labelledby="ssuper-motion"><p class="ssuper-index">{chapters[0].index}</p><h2 id="ssuper-motion">{chapters[0].title}</h2><p class="ssuper-discipline">{chapters[0].discipline}</p><p class="ssuper-chapter-copy">{chapters[0].copy}</p><figure class="ssuper-media"><img src={`${asset}karoo.png`} alt="Road through the Karoo landscape" width="1024" height="683" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></figure><figure class="ssuper-media ssuper-archive-detail"><img src={`${asset}archive-01.png`} alt="Close detail from the living archive" width="576" height="1024" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></figure></section>

    <section class="ssuper-chapter" aria-labelledby="ssuper-archive"><p class="ssuper-index">{chapters[1].index}</p><h2 id="ssuper-archive">{chapters[1].title}</h2><p class="ssuper-discipline">{chapters[1].discipline}</p><p class="ssuper-chapter-copy">{chapters[1].copy}</p><figure class="ssuper-media"><img src={`${asset}archive-02.png`} alt="Archive visual study" width="3600" height="2192" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></figure></section>

    <section class="ssuper-chapter" aria-labelledby="ssuper-words"><p class="ssuper-index">03 / RELATIONAL MAPPING</p><h2 id="ssuper-words">WHEN WORDS BECOME MATERIAL.</h2><p class="ssuper-discipline">RELATIONAL MAPPING / SEMANTIC MASK / VISUAL STUDIES</p><figure class="ssuper-media"><img src={`${asset}document.png`} alt="Relational word mapping charts" width="1502" height="702" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></figure></section>

    <section class="ssuper-chapter" aria-labelledby="ssuper-interface"><p class="ssuper-index">{chapters[2].index}</p><h2 id="ssuper-interface">{chapters[2].title}</h2><p class="ssuper-discipline">{chapters[2].discipline}</p><p class="ssuper-chapter-copy">{chapters[2].copy}</p><figure class="ssuper-video-composition"><img src={`${asset}alice-video-poster.png`} alt="Masked figure in the Project Alice visual study" width="1350" height="786" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /><figcaption class="ssuper-glass"><img src={`${asset}superlative-mark.png`} alt="" width="69" height="54" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /><span>SSUPERLATIVE / ALICE / 05.00</span></figcaption></figure><figure class="ssuper-media ssuper-study"><img src={`${asset}alice-film-still.png`} alt="Project Alice research drawing" width="1006" height="1024" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></figure></section>

    <section class="ssuper-chapter" aria-labelledby="ssuper-product"><p class="ssuper-index">{chapters[3].index}</p><h2 id="ssuper-product">{chapters[3].title}</h2><p class="ssuper-discipline">{chapters[3].discipline}</p><p class="ssuper-chapter-copy">{chapters[3].copy}</p></section>

    <section class="ssuper-chapter" aria-labelledby="ssuper-becoming"><p class="ssuper-index">{chapters[4].index}</p><h2 id="ssuper-becoming">{chapters[4].title}</h2><p class="ssuper-discipline">{chapters[4].discipline}</p><p class="ssuper-chapter-copy">{chapters[4].copy}</p></section>
  </div>
</div>

<style>
  .ssuper-revised{background:#fff;color:#141414;padding:200px var(--gutter) 120px}.ssuper-inner{max-width:1344px;margin:auto;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:96px}.ssuper-media{margin:0;overflow:hidden}.ssuper-media img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto}.ssuper-rope{aspect-ratio:1344/922}.ssuper-rope img{height:100%;object-fit:cover}.ssuper-opening{font:400 clamp(72px,9vw,144px)/1.05 var(--font-display);text-transform:uppercase}.ssuper-copy-row{display:grid;grid-template-columns:330px minmax(0,1fr);gap:60px}.ssuper-copy-row span,.ssuper-index,.ssuper-discipline{font-size:12px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.08em;line-height:1.6}.ssuper-copy-row p{max-width:930px;font-size:24px;line-height:1.54}.ssuper-chapter{display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:flex-start;gap:24px;padding-top:24px}.ssuper-chapter h2{font:400 clamp(44px,5vw,60px)/1.05 var(--font-display);text-transform:uppercase}.ssuper-index,.ssuper-discipline{color:#666}.ssuper-chapter-copy{max-width:930px;font-size:20px;line-height:1.55;margin:16px 0}.ssuper-chapter>.ssuper-media,.ssuper-chapter>.ssuper-video-composition{width:100%;margin-top:16px}.ssuper-archive-detail{max-height:661px}.ssuper-archive-detail img{height:661px;object-fit:cover}.ssuper-video-composition{position:relative;aspect-ratio:1350/786;overflow:hidden;background:#101820}.ssuper-video-composition::after{content:"";position:absolute;inset:0;pointer-events:none;background:linear-gradient(to right,transparent 24.95%,#ffffff33 25%,transparent 25.05%,transparent 74.95%,#ffffff33 75%,transparent 75.05%)}.ssuper-video-composition>img{display:block;width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover}.ssuper-glass{position:absolute;z-index:1;left:7.4%;right:7.4%;top:2%;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:16px;min-height:70px;border-bottom:1px solid #ffffff80;color:#fff;font:12px/1.3 monospace;letter-spacing:.08em;background:#ffffff0c;backdrop-filter:blur(10px);-webkit-backdrop-filter:blur(10px)}.ssuper-glass img{width:69px;height:54px;object-fit:contain}.ssuper-study{max-width:500px;background:#e3e3e3}
  @media(max-width:767px){.ssuper-revised{padding:64px var(--gutter)}.ssuper-inner{gap:56px}.ssuper-copy-row{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:16px}.ssuper-copy-row p{font-size:18px;line-height:1.5}.ssuper-chapter-copy{font-size:18px;line-height:1.5}.ssuper-opening{font-size:clamp(60px,13vw,96px)}.ssuper-glass{min-height:48px;font-size:8px;gap:8px}.ssuper-glass img{width:44px;height:34px}}
</style>
